{"term":"flock","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5d13905c04310bb26f","definition":"A number of birds together in a group, such as those gathered together for the purpose of migration.","example":"He told his father, and said it would be just suitable work for him to run about fields and woods amongst the strawberry hills after a flock of hares, and now and then lie down and take a nap on some sunny hill.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bunch","gaggle","horde","host","legion","litter","nest","rabble","swarm","throng","wake"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"collective","register":"collective","wordFamily":["flerd","flock camera","flocker","flockful","flockless","flocklike","flockling","flockmaster","flockmate","flockmeal","flockowner","flockwise","flocky","flower of the flock","species flock","subflock"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flock#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a3bb609fec1f99e9e1","definition":"Those served by a particular pastor or shepherd.","example":"But lapsed into so long a pause again / As half amazed, half frighted all his flock: [...]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bunch","gaggle","horde","host","legion","litter","nest","rabble","swarm","throng","wake"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["flerd","flock camera","flocker","flockful","flockless","flocklike","flockling","flockmaster","flockmate","flockmeal","flockowner","flockwise","flocky","flower of the flock","species flock","subflock"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flock#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0b141e6e908d3ebbb5","definition":"To congregate in or head towards a place in large numbers.","example":"People flocked to the cinema to see the new film.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","regi